e after maintenance and could add severe loss. The abrupt complete loss of all channels is much more characteristic of a pulled patch than a soft dirty-connector fault.", "grounded": ["oms.S19-S06"], "n_grounded": 1, "note": ""}, {"fault_mode": "AMP_PUMP_FAIL", "location_kind": "shared", "term": null, "anchor_symptom": null, "anchor_service": null, "element": "E28", "probability": 0.01, "rationale": "A failed booster could remove all downstream channels. However, its input should remain visible and its pump-current telemetry should change, whereas booster input power was lost and pump current showed no change.", "grounded": ["oms.S19-S06.amp0"], "n_grounded": 1, "note": ""}], "probability_other": 0.03, "sum_stated": 0.98}, "llm": {"provider": "openai", "model": "gpt-5.6"}, "llm_calls": [{"role": "proposer", "latency_s": 18.44313406944275, "input_tokens": 20597, "output_tokens": 1531, "reasoning_tokens": 963, "ok": true, "error": ""}]}